From 1d7d470763434ff7fe6102d3e43616d17d3fb121 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 07:43:28 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(post): post a short arc whose written ends share one
 angle as a line

PR #3471 stops an arc block whose written end is its written start. One
case stayed: the written ends differ only along the radial line through
the written centre. A control that reads the sweep from the end angles
then sees no sweep, or a full turn (a spiral of nearly one turn).

arcFateOf now reads the written start, end and centre words. When the
written end is on the written start's ray from the centre (or one end is
on the centre) and the record turns half a circle or less, the record
posts as the script's straight feed move. The test uses only the zero of
the cross product and the sign of the dot product, so mirrored or scaled
words (a lathe diameter) read the same. The two lathes now write that
feed move in their meridian arc path.

Fixes #3474

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
